{"cluster_id": "C-2024", "topic": "zero-trust LIST discovery", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B033-073", "B033-079", "B037-020", "B038-007"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS GC trust chain is catalog cut, `_ckpt` acknowledged frontier, exact `GET` records, and conditional-write fences; LIST is only a hint for work bounds, witness sets, and genesis. CAS GC optimization must retain arithmetic middle intake everywhere, frontier probes for held or logless namespaces, and `tail < cursor` quality detection; only `tail == cursor` can prove a trusted frontier under a bucket passport. Under the amended v9 intake, `LIST` is a zero-trust hint; fold progress advances arithmetically and destructive work requires a per-namespace frontier proof. GC must not trust LIST completeness, independently of whether the object store is RustFS or AWS S3.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-03-list-trust-verdict.md#optimization-scope", "docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-03-list-trust-verdict.md#trusted-verbs", "docs/superpowers/models/CaRefDeltaIntakeCore_RESULTS.md#L86-L90", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-26-list-incompleteness-proof/README.md#limits"]}
