{"cluster_id": "C-2030", "topic": "attempt-scoped GC artifacts", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B035-005", "B043-017"], "canonical_claim": "The concurrent-leader GC fix stores every per-round artifact, including `retired` and `outcomes`, under `gc/gen/<gen>/attempt/<a>/...`, where `<a>` is the folding leader's lease sequence; a lease-guarded adopt CAS publishes `(snap_generation, snap_attempt)`, and readers resolve only that adopted pair. All decision-bearing GC artifacts, including `retired` and `outcomes`, are under `gc/gen/<g>/attempt/<a>/`, and only the adopted attempt is reader-visible.", "issue_ids": ["GC-CONCURRENT-LEADER-LEAK", "S33"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/how-we-got-here.md#turn-attempt-scoped", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L74-L74"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2031", "topic": "GC cadence should be driven by", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B035-015"], "canonical_claim": "GC cadence should be driven by per-shard journal pressure (event count, body size, or age), not changed-shard count, because one hot shard can accumulate thousands of mutations while still counting as one changed shard.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L971-L1008"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2032", "topic": "The GC wedge fix protects pending", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B035-041"], "canonical_claim": "The GC-wedge fix protects pending removals of every owner kind: in `activeManifestKeys`, any removal with `transition_version > sealedFoldCursor` keeps its `old_binding` manifest body active until the removal `-1` is sealed; the sweep also emits a manifest-delete audit event.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L1730-L1848"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2033", "topic": "The B140 dangle fix requires both", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B036-001", "B036-004"], "canonical_claim": "The B140 dangle fix requires both `TrimGated`, which limits journal trimming to the committed fold cursor, and `CursorInSnap`, which atomically commits the fold cursor with the snap edges.; The merged `m_merged` configuration was green with `TrimGated = TRUE` and `CursorInSnap = TRUE`, while `m_both_buggy`, `m_cursorskip`, and `m_trimonly` violated `INV_NO_LOSS` under the same bounds.", "issue_ids": ["B140"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaB140DangleMerge_RESULTS.md#ca-b140-dangle-merge-results", "docs/superpowers/models/CaB140DangleMerge_RESULTS.md#per-configuration-evidence"]}
